[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137597,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Signet-ring cell&nbsp;/ histiocytoid carcinoma is an aggressive adnexal neoplasm composed of neoplastic cells with signet-ring or histiocytoid morphology that diffusely involves the dermis and subcutis of the eyelid.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137598,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8490/3 Signet-ring cell&nbsp;/ histiocytoid carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137599,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C33 &amp; XH0XE5 Adnexal carcinoma of skin &amp; Signet ring cell/histiocytoid carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137600,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> monocle tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137601,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137602,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dermis and subcutis in the eyelid and periocular skin</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137603,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Signet-ring cell&nbsp;/ histiocytoid carcinoma is most common in elderly men, where it presents insidiously as painless swelling, often affecting both upper and lower eyelids, and sometimes simulating periorbital oedema {30976586;33054772;33315842;34923671}, and can lead to a monocle appearance. The nonspecific nature of the clinical features can frequently lead to delayed diagnosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137604,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour has an M:F&nbsp;ratio of about 4:1 {21317710}. The reported age range is 42&ndash;87&nbsp;years, with a median patient age of 66&nbsp;years {21317710}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137605,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137606,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Next-generation sequencing has shown mutations in <em>CDH1</em>, the gene encoding E-cadherin {32358805;33617508;34804623}. Mutations in this gene are known to confer signet-ring morphology in other carcinomas. Mutations in <em>NTRK3</em>, <em>p27</em> (<em>CDKN1B</em>),<em> ERBB2</em>,<em> TP53</em>, and <em>PIK3CA</em> have also been detected {33617508}. It is suggested that mutations particularly in <em>CDH1 </em>induce E-cadherin dysfunction which may play a role in tumour progression.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137607,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In exenteration specimens there may be a poorly defined periocular mass often involving both upper and lower eyelids. Complete surgical resection may be difficult to accomplish given the single-file nature of tumour cells and thus difficulty in achieving negative margins with conservative surgery.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137608,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is composed of signet-ring or histiocytoid epithelial cells (exhibit eosinophilic granular cytoplasm) which diffusely infiltrate the collagen bundles of the dermis with sparing of the epidermis. The tumour cells may show a single-file pattern. Immunohistochemical staining is positive for cytokeratins (pancytokeratin and CK7). Staining is positive for GATA3, EMA (MUC1), MUC5AC, and AR, and with BerEP4 {34156717}. GCDFP-15 and E-cadherin stain positive in the majority of cases {33054772}. ER and PR are variably expressed {30976586}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Metastatic breast lobular carcinoma and gastrointestinal adenocarcinomas with a signet-ring cell morphology are the main differential diagnoses. Immunohistochemistry (negative staining for CDX2 and CK20) is helpful to confirm a skin primary. However, a full clinical assessment is essential to rule out breast and gastrointestinal primaries.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137609,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are no reports of cytology.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137610,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>CDH1</em> mutations are not in routine use to assist diagnosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137611,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> diffuse infiltrate of signet-ring or histiocytoid cells; exclusion of metastatic signet ring carcinoma from other sites.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> immunohistochemical expression of cytokeratins and AR.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137612,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) and the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM system for non-melanoma eyelid carcinoma applies.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137613,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 66,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are limited data, owing to the small number of cases. Treatment usually requires exenteration with or without adjuvant radiotherapy. About of one&nbsp;third of cases are reported to develop metastasis over a 10-year follow-up period {33054772}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:59:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]